<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Cossack Hetmanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1649 CE – 1764 CE · capital Chyhyryn</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Cossack state created by Bohdan Khmelnytsky's uprising, which governed central Ukraine under hetmans until Catherine the Great abolished it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1648 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a> led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaporozhian-cossacks">Zaporozhian Cossacks</a> and peasants in a rebellion against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. After victories at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-zhovti-vody">Zhovti Vody</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chersonesus-taurica">Korsun</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-zboriv">Treaty of Zboriv</a> in 1649 recognised a Cossack-ruled territory with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chyhyryn">Chyhyryn</a>. In 1654, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pereiaslav">Pereiaslav</a>, Khmelnytsky accepted the protection of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tsardom-of-russia">Tsardom of Russia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Hetmanate was divided into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> regiments that served as both military and administrative units, led by an elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">hetman</a> and a council of senior officers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> culture flourished, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv-mohyla-academy">Kyiv-Mohyla Academy</a> as its intellectual centre. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Khmelnytsky</a>'s death, the period called the Ruin brought civil war and division along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truce-of-andrusovo">Truce of Andrusovo</a> in 1667.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-mazepa">Ivan Mazepa</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII of Sweden</a>, and after their defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> in 1709 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> steadily reduced the Hetmanate's autonomy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine II</a> forced the last hetman, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyrylo-rozumovsky">Kyrylo Rozumovsky</a>, to resign in 1764, and the regimental system was abolished by 1781.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cossack-hetmanate.jpg" alt="Cossack Hetmanate" width="320" height="189"><figcaption>Image: Yetti · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hetmanate_Army_flag.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1649 CE – 1764 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chyhyryn</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bohdan Khmelnytsky, Ivan Mazepa, Kyrylo Rozumovsky</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ukrainian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hetmanate, Zaporozhian Host, Little Russia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1706&amp;focus=cossack-hetmanate" aria-label="Cossack Hetmanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5434 465 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cossack Hetmanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5754 721L5818 759M5754 721L5457 693M5754 721L5820 533M5754 721L5709 970M5754 721L6487 457"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5818 759h0M5457 693h0M5820 533h0M5709 970h0M6487 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d